# Host values: text that identifies one host.
#
# scripts/scan.sh reports each line that contains one of these patterns.
# A finding fails on the branch portable, on a tag portable-v* and in the
# publisher; it is a warning on other branches (docs/secret-handling.md).
#
# This file is tracked and published, so it holds generic patterns only. A
# pattern of a real host would put that host value into the tree that it
# forbids. The patterns of one host go into the untracked file
# .local/host-values.deny (same format). The scan stops when that file is
# absent or empty, unless --allow-no-local-deny is given (a public clone).
# scripts/host-values.regex gives the address rules.
# scripts/host-values.allow gives the exceptions.
#
# Format: one literal pattern for each line, case-insensitive. A line that
# starts with "#" is a comment. Quotes and backslashes are not allowed.
# The scan does not report host values in this file and in
# .local/host-values.deny.
